# Trivy vulnerability-scan exception list for the production container image.
#
# Policy (enforced by .github/workflows/ci.yml -> "Scan final image ..."):
#   * The build FAILS on EVERY HIGH or CRITICAL OS or application vulnerability
#     in the final image — fixed OR unfixed (`ignore-unfixed: false`).
#   * The ONLY way to pass with a known HIGH/CRITICAL finding is to add its
#     exact CVE id below, with a complete justification block. Broad severity
#     or "unfixed" suppression is not permitted.
#   * Do NOT add an entry merely to make CI go green. If a finding cannot be
#     accepted, bump the pinned base-image digest / dependency instead.
#
# Required fields for every exception (all mandatory):
#   # CVE-XXXX-YYYYY
#   #   Package:    <name@version>
#   #   Reason:     why this specific CVE does not apply to how we run the image
#   #   Risk:       residual risk assessment (impact x exploitability here)
#   #   Approved-by: <name / role> on <YYYY-MM-DD>
#   #   Review-by:  <YYYY-MM-DD>   (re-evaluate or remove on/before this date)
#   CVE-XXXX-YYYYY
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# APPROVED EXCEPTIONS: none.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
